The singleton of the principal element of a neighbourhood X equals the principal element of the power domain generated by the down-set of X.

By extensionality, singleton membership gives a neighbourhood Y of the principal element, a power-domain neighbourhood, and an inclusion of the down-set of Y. The down-set criterion turns the principal inclusion of X in Y into an inclusion of the down-set of X in the down-set of Y, which composes to an inclusion in the given power-domain neighbourhood. Conversely, X itself, with the reflexive inclusion, is the singleton witness for that same power-domain neighbourhood.
